Vendored code
-------------

Two files in this plugin are copied verbatim from the PromptFixer project
(https://github.com/Osman19702/PromptFixer), MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Osman
Turalioglu. Same author, same licence; they are vendored so the plugin runs
standalone with no install, no network and no dependency on a PromptFixer
checkout.

  plugin file                    upstream path in PromptFixer
  -----------------------------  ------------------------------
  scripts/analyze.js             server/analyze.js
  scripts/promptfixer-lint.js    scripts/lint-prompts.js

Vendored 2026-09-24 from PromptFixer 0.3.0.

scripts/promptfixer-lint.js carries exactly three modifications, all of them
consequences of the rename. One makes the renamed sibling resolve:

  -  import { analyzePrompt } from '../server/analyze.js'
  +  import { analyzePrompt } from './analyze.js'

The other two are usage text, in the header comment and in the USAGE
constant, so that --help names the file the user actually runs:

  -  node scripts/lint-prompts.js <path...> ...
  +  node scripts/promptfixer-lint.js <path...> ...

No logic differs. scripts/analyze.js is byte-identical to its upstream
original. Neither file was reformatted.

scripts/package.json is not vendored. It exists only to mark these two files
as ES modules when the plugin is installed outside a Node package.

Checking for drift
------------------

  node scripts/check-vendored.mjs [path-to-PromptFixer-checkout]

It compares both files against upstream, allows only the three enumerated
differences above, and exits 0 in sync, 1 on drift, 2 when a file it needs is
missing. The upstream root defaults to $PROMPTFIXER_DIR, else a PromptFixer
checkout beside this repository.
